# Plain-English errors and logs

Yash is a designer, not a coder. Every log, thrown error, and on-screen message must use everyday words a 5th grader can follow. Say what broke, why, and where. A status code alone is not an explanation.

Each error includes:

1. **What** the person was trying to do
2. **Why** it failed, in words (keep the status code for the machine, and say what it means)
3. **File** that failed, full path
4. **Connected to** other files or services in the chain, when the failure crosses a boundary
5. **Fix** — one next step

On screen, stay short. Put the file path and connections in the log, not in a stack trace on the page.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — code only, no place, no cause
return NextResponse.json({ error: "404" }, { status: 404 });
catch (e) { console.error(e); }

// ✅ GOOD
return NextResponse.json({
  error: "Page not found. No screen in the app uses this address.",
  file: "src/app/campaigns/[id]/page.tsx",
  connectedTo: "src/services/campaigns.ts looks up the campaign in Supabase",
  fix: "Check the campaign link, or open Campaigns from the sidebar.",
}, { status: 404 });

logError({
  what: "Could not pause the campaign.",
  why: "Supabase has no campaign with this id, so nothing was changed.",
  file: "src/features/campaigns/services/pause-campaign.ts",
  connectedTo: "src/lib/ai/parse-command.ts sent this action from the copilot.",
  fix: "Open the preview card and confirm the campaign still exists.",
  cause: error,
});
```

Map codes in words: 404 page not found, 401 not signed in, 403 not allowed, 409 already done, 429 too many tries, 500 something inside the app broke.
